.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_WORKER_DATAFLOW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_worker_dataflow ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_new_standalone ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_free ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_index ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_peers ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_step ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_step_or_park ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_step_while ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_has_dataflows ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_drop_dataflow ,
.Nm dtfl_worker_next_dataflow_index
.Nd build and drive dataflows on a worker
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_worker_dataflow "dtfl_worker *w" "const char *name" "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "dtfl_build_fn build" "void *ctx"
.Ft dtfl_worker *
.Fn dtfl_worker_new_standalone "void"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_worker_free "dtfl_worker *w"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_worker_index "const dtfl_worker *w"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_worker_peers "const dtfl_worker *w"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_worker_step "dtfl_worker *w"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_worker_step_or_park "dtfl_worker *w" "uint64_t timeout_ns"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_worker_step_while "dtfl_worker *w" "bool (*cond)(void *ctx)" "void *ctx"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_worker_has_dataflows "const dtfl_worker *w"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_worker_drop_dataflow "dtfl_worker *w" "size_t index"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_worker_next_dataflow_index "const dtfl_worker *w"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A worker owns a share of the computation.
Inside the function passed to
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ,
or on a worker from
.Fn dtfl_worker_new_standalone ,
.Fn dtfl_worker_dataflow
builds one dataflow:
it calls
.Fa build
with a root scope over the timestamp class
.Fa tc
and the given
.Fa ctx ,
installs the resulting operators, and returns.
.Fa name
labels the dataflow in logs.
The index the dataflow will receive is
.Fn dtfl_worker_next_dataflow_index .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_worker_index
is this worker's position in
.Bq 0 , Fn dtfl_worker_peers ,
the number of workers in the computation.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_worker_step
runs each active dataflow once and returns whether any dataflow
remains.
.Fn dtfl_worker_step_or_park
is the same but, when nothing is runnable, parks the thread for up to
.Fa timeout_ns
nanoseconds
.Pq Dv UINT64_MAX waits without limit
or until another thread wakes it.
.Fn dtfl_worker_step_while
steps while
.Fa cond
returns true.
.Fn dtfl_worker_has_dataflows
reports whether any dataflow is still running.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_worker_drop_dataflow
removes the dataflow with the given
.Fa index .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_worker_new_standalone
creates a single-worker handle that the caller steps by hand, outside
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ;
.Fn dtfl_worker_free
releases it.
Only a standalone worker may be freed this way; a worker passed to an
.Xr dtfl_execute 3
callback is owned by the runtime.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_worker_dataflow
returns 0 on success or one of the errors below.
.Fn dtfl_worker_new_standalone
returns a worker, or aborts through the panic hook on allocation
failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_worker *w = dtfl_worker_new_standalone();
dtfl_worker_dataflow(w, "example", tc, build, NULL);
while (dtfl_worker_has_dataflows(w))
	dtfl_worker_step(w);
dtfl_worker_free(w);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_ESTATE
.It Bq Er DTFL_ESTATE
.Fn dtfl_worker_dataflow
was called from inside an operator.
.It Bq Er DTFL_EINVAL
.Fa tc
does not refine the unit class.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_config 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_scope_scoped 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These correspond to timely's
.Vt Worker
methods
.Fn dataflow ,
.Fn step ,
.Fn step_or_park
and the threadless-example standalone worker.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A worker belongs to one thread.
All of these functions must be called from that thread.
To wake a parked worker from another thread, use its sync activator.
